WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:20.473
Jack floundered in the deep end of the community pool while Coach Shin, Laura, and Mrs.

2
00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:23.194
Wilson took turns pushing his head under water.

3
00:00:26.195 --> 00:00:28.476
As Jack struggled for his life, Mrs.

4
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:32.406
Wilson shouted at him, "Cup your hands, young man!"

5
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:37.069
Jack sprang up, flung his arms out, and fought his attackers.

6
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.731
Oh. There were no attackers.

7
00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:44.934
Jack was in bed, waking up from a terrible nightmare.

8
00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:50.078
He turned on his phone to check the time: it was only five o'clock in the morning.

9
00:00:51.138 --> 00:00:56.762
In the LED glow, he saw Luke with his thumb in his mouth, fast asleep under his superhero

10
00:00:56.822 --> 00:01:02.290
bedspread. He was so cute—during the rare times he wasn't talking or moving.

11
00:01:03.691 --> 00:01:10.336
Jack closed his eyes and tried hard to get back to sleep, but his mind was wide-awake, whirling

12
00:01:10.396 --> 00:01:11.837
with worries and thoughts.

13
00:01:12.878 --> 00:01:16.321
At five thirty Jack took his phone into the bathroom and called Noah.

14
00:01:17.061 --> 00:01:18.963
It was two hours later in Oklahoma.

15
00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:25.428
Noah would probably be awake; swim team practice always started early on summer mornings.

16
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.641
After the third ring, Noah greeted him with a groggy, "Huh?

17
00:01:31.381 --> 00:01:33.722
Jack?" "Did I wake you up?"

18
00:01:34.082 --> 00:01:36.223
Jack asked, though he knew he had.

19
00:01:37.003 --> 00:01:38.504
Noah yawned in response.

20
00:01:44.185 --> 00:01:44.685
Jack said.

21
00:01:44.705 --> 00:01:47.206
"I really need a friend to talk to."

22
00:01:47.226 --> 00:01:48.807
"What's wrong?"

23
00:01:49.247 --> 00:01:49.947
Noah asked.

24
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.508
The whole story came out in a rush.

25
00:01:54.304 --> 00:02:00.629
Jack told Noah about his family's tiny apartment and his humiliating first swim practice with the Sharks.

26
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.193
Jack took a deep breath and blurted out more of his misery.

27
00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:11.418
"And then the pretty girl in my apartment building told my mother I hadn't been at practices.

28
00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:15.561
My parents made me clean the kitchen and apologize to my coach.

29
00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:18.344
And now he won't let me compete at the next meet.

30
00:02:18.784 --> 00:02:19.765
It stinks, right?"

31
00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:23.388
On the other end Noah stayed silent.

32
00:02:24.328 --> 00:02:25.789
"Noah? Are you still there?"

33
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.491
Jack finally asked.

34
00:02:27.511 --> 00:02:30.413
"Yeah," Noah said.

35
00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:32.835
"Sorry you have to share a room with Luke.

36
00:02:33.315 --> 00:02:36.058
The kid is cute, but he can get annoying sometimes."

37
00:02:36.078 --> 00:02:37.419
"I know.

38
00:02:38.059 --> 00:02:41.462
Plus, my new swim team is a nightmare," Jack repeated.

39
00:02:41.482 --> 00:02:45.325
"This guy everyone calls Hulk is like Michael Phelps.

40
00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.847
He's got muscles on top of his muscles!"

41
00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:50.129
More silence.

42
00:02:51.089 --> 00:02:53.992
"Thanks for the sympathy," Jack said sarcastically.

43
00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:57.105
"You want my sympathy for not being the number one swimmer?"

44
00:02:57.586 --> 00:02:58.206
Noah asked.

45
00:02:58.226 --> 00:03:01.908
"I've never been the best on our team.

46
00:03:02.509 --> 00:03:03.449
You were always better.

47
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.471
Jacob and Mark are better swimmers than I am too.

48
00:03:06.971 --> 00:03:07.471
Big deal."

49
00:03:08.132 --> 00:03:09.873
Now Noah was being sarcastic.

50
00:03:09.893 --> 00:03:13.975
"It's not just that," Jack mumbled.

51
00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:16.317
"I have to miss the first swim meet.

52
00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:18.878
It's a big one too, against the team's biggest rival."

53
00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.840
"You did ditch practice, Jack.

54
00:03:22.464 --> 00:03:26.125
You know that Coach Rayder wouldn't let you compete either if you missed several practices."

55
00:03:27.085 --> 00:03:28.626
Jack stayed silent this time.

56
00:03:28.646 --> 00:03:31.667
"I'm sorry things aren't going well for you," Noah said.

57
00:03:31.687 --> 00:03:34.687
"But there will be more swim meets this summer, right?"

58
00:03:34.707 --> 00:03:37.648
"Yeah," Jack muttered.

59
00:03:38.368 --> 00:03:39.649
"The season is just starting."

60
00:03:40.109 --> 00:03:40.629
He paused.

61
00:03:40.649 --> 00:03:43.650
"I guess I sound kind of whiny, huh?"

62
00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.210
More silence.

63
00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.611
"Okay, more than kind of whiny.

64
00:03:49.651 --> 00:03:51.932
I sound completely whiny," Jack said.

65
00:03:53.108 --> 00:03:54.269
"Yep," Noah said.

66
00:03:54.289 --> 00:03:58.570
"Stop feeling sorry for yourself, and just work on improving your swimming.

67
00:03:59.011 --> 00:04:01.652
I bet it'll all work out fine, even with that pretty girl."

68
00:04:01.672 --> 00:04:04.173
"Thanks, Noah," Jack said.

69
00:04:04.193 --> 00:04:07.214
"Speaking of girls, how are things with Kara?"

70
00:04:08.474 --> 00:04:09.155
Noah groaned.

71
00:04:09.175 --> 00:04:15.617
"We had one date—just one dumb date—and now she thinks I'm her boyfriend.

72
00:04:16.678 --> 00:04:18.459
She texts me a thousand times a day.

73
00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:21.840
If I don't text back right away, she calls me to ask what's wrong.

74
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.582
And if I don't pick up her calls, she texts some more."

75
00:04:24.602 --> 00:04:26.563
"Ugh," Jack said.

76
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:28.184
"That sounds awful."

77
00:04:28.204 --> 00:04:31.847
"It is awful," Noah said.

78
00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:34.028
"Sorry, but I have to go now.

79
00:04:34.348 --> 00:04:35.789
I have to get ready for swim practice.

80
00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.050
Good talking to you, Jack."

81
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.712
"You too," Jack said.

82
00:04:40.573 --> 00:04:42.134
"Thanks for listening to all my complaints."

83
00:04:42.154 --> 00:04:43.475
"Good luck.

84
00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:45.836
And take my advice," Noah went on.

85
00:04:45.856 --> 00:04:50.439
"Don't give any girls your phone number, unless you want to spend all your time answering their texts

86
00:04:50.519 --> 00:04:51.020
and calls."

87
00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.560
Jack laughed.

88
00:04:53.821 --> 00:04:57.361
"That's probably really good advice," he said.

89
00:04:57.902 --> 00:05:00.442
Although he couldn't picture Laura texting him all the time.

90
00:05:01.643 --> 00:05:04.623
After they hung up, Jack thought about what Noah had said.

91
00:05:05.784 --> 00:05:07.544
Noah really did have some good points.

92
00:05:08.164 --> 00:05:11.385
Jack had to stop whining and start focusing on his swimming.

93
00:05:12.246 --> 00:05:13.806
Jack was glad he'd called Noah.

94
00:05:15.226 --> 00:05:17.587
A few minutes later, Jack got into his swimsuit.

95
00:05:18.947 --> 00:05:20.728
A swim would help him figure things out.

96
00:05:21.536 --> 00:05:25.277
He was hoping that there would be another swimmer there, but not crabby Mrs.

97
00:05:25.317 --> 00:05:29.718
Wilson. Jack left a note for his parents and hurried out of the apartment.

98
00:05:32.179 --> 00:05:34.059
But when he got to the pool, Mrs.

99
00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:38.561
Wilson was the only swimmer in the pool, floating on her back in the deep end.

100
00:05:39.421 --> 00:05:43.422
In her colorful bathing suit, her body resembled a huge beach ball.

101
00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.983
"Oh well," Jack thought.

102
00:05:46.603 --> 00:05:50.924
He waved at her half-heartedly before diving in and doing a few freestyle laps.

103
00:05:56.349 --> 00:05:57.530
When he stopped, Mrs.

104
00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:02.931
Wilson said, "Great job cupping your hands—if you were doing the breaststroke.

105
00:06:03.671 --> 00:06:07.733
You have to keep your hands cupped the whole time for the freestyle stroke.

106
00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:11.814
And you're not dropping your head enough to breathe properly.

107
00:06:12.474 --> 00:06:15.915
You should see my grandson do the butterfly.

108
00:06:16.715 --> 00:06:19.736
Little Tommy is like beauty in motion.

109
00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:24.043
The way he breathes—" "Grr!"

110
00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:25.183
Jack thought.

111
00:06:25.824 --> 00:06:27.845
He dived underwater and swam away.

112
00:06:30.327 --> 00:06:35.250
After a few strokes, just out of curiosity, he cupped his hands the way Mrs.

113
00:06:35.291 --> 00:06:36.391
Wilson had advised.

114
00:06:39.473 --> 00:06:43.937
Once again his stroke did seem smoother after he followed her advice.

115
00:06:44.657 --> 00:06:46.178
He tried lowering his head a bit.

116
00:06:46.518 --> 00:06:47.979
That seemed to make him faster.

117
00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.721
He swam to the shallow end of the pool.

118
00:06:56.742 --> 00:06:57.622
Maybe having Mrs.

119
00:06:57.662 --> 00:06:59.163
Wilson around wasn't so bad.

120
00:07:00.203 --> 00:07:03.185
He wondered how she knew so much about swimming techniques.

121
00:07:03.965 --> 00:07:07.867
He glanced at where she'd been floating on her back, but she was no longer there.

122
00:07:09.507 --> 00:07:10.608
He looked at the pool deck.

123
00:07:11.308 --> 00:07:12.349
She wasn't there either.

124
00:07:13.569 --> 00:07:16.470
Jack finally had the pool all to himself.

125
00:07:17.231 --> 00:07:20.472
He gazed happily across the glistening, peaceful water.

126
00:07:21.772 --> 00:07:23.113
"Ah," he said aloud.

127
00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:29.316
"Peace." Then he noticed a large, bright mass on the bottom of the pool.

128
00:07:30.076 --> 00:07:30.837
He stared at it.

129
00:07:31.677 --> 00:07:34.559
Not it—her—Mrs.

130
00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:37.060
Wilson. She wasn't moving.

131
00:07:38.401 --> 00:07:38.841
"Oh no!"

132
00:07:39.261 --> 00:07:39.901
Jack cried.

133
00:07:40.462 --> 00:07:44.164
Mrs. Wilson looked like she was unconscious or dead!
